    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Yordan Alvarez** (85.52) and **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (82.12) headlining our offensive attack. **Yordan Alvarez** remains our premier power threat, capitalizing on a favorable matchup against Brandon Young, whose 4.66 xERA provides a soft landing for **Yordan Alvarez**\u2019s elite 0.477 xwOBA. Simultaneously, we are leaning heavily into stolen base upside with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** and **Christian Yelich** (66.17). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits from an excellent 100% stolen base expectation against Zebby Matthews, while **Christian Yelich** draws a massive +13% platoon boost against Eury P\u00e9rez, turning what could have been a pedestrian outing into a high-leverage start.\n\nThe most challenging decision today involved our bench, where **Chase Meidroth** (52.83) narrowly missed the final cut. While **Chase Meidroth** offered a respectable floor, he ultimately fell short due to an assumed #9 batting order slot, which severely hampered his run-scoring potential compared to the middle-of-the-order security offered by **Nelson Velazquez** (66.15) and **Colt Keith** (69.64). **Colt Keith** is particularly well-positioned today; his +7% platoon advantage and prime #3 spot in the lineup against Ryan Johnson make him a stronger play than **Dillon Dingler** (52.02), who faces the same starter but is burdened by a -15% dynamic platoon penalty.\n\nManagers should remain vigilant regarding the status of the lineup card, as all projections are currently pinned to \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. The risk profile is highest for **Trea Turner** (57.77) and **Kyle Schwarber** (55.17), both of whom are facing Nolan McLean. While McLean\u2019s 3.49 xERA represents a stiff challenge that suppresses their base projections, their placement in the #1 and #2 spots respectively provides enough volume to keep them in our starting group. We are prioritizing efficiency over raw power today, keeping **Kazuma Okamoto** (47.36) and **Gary Sanchez** (45.13) in the lineup primarily for their situational context, but we will monitor any pinch-hitting risks that could force a late swap with bench options like **Carson Benge** (51.46) should the wind or weather shifts negatively impact park factors.",
